// This file contains test cases regarding issue 179
// (https://github.com/kkew3/jieba.vim/issues/179).
//
// Best viewed in Vim.

#V 5

## Builtin behaviors
#X i
#B0 |aaa␊bbb␊

// Unnamed inline yank goes to "0 and "".
K y;w X
B1 aaa␊bbb␊0:aaa␊1:␊-:␊a:␊":aaa␊

// Unnamed multiline yank goes to "0 and "".
K y2;w X
B1 aaa␊bbb␊0:aaa␊bbb␊1:␊-:␊a:␊":aaa␊bbb␊

// Named inline yank goes to the named register and "".
K "ay;w X
B1 aaa␊bbb␊0:␊1:␊-:␊a:aaa␊":aaa␊

// Named multiline yank goes to the named register and "".
K "ay2;w X
B1 aaa␊bbb␊0:␊1:␊-:␊a:aaa␊bbb␊":aaa␊bbb␊

// Unnamed inline delete goes to "- and "".
K d;w X
B1 ␊bbb␊0:␊1:␊-:aaa␊a:␊":aaa␊

// Unnamed multiline delete goes to "1 and "".
K d2;w X
B1 ␊0:␊1:aaa␊bbb␊-:␊a:␊":aaa␊bbb␊

// Named inline delete goes to the named register and "".
K "ad;w X
B1 ␊bbb␊0:␊1:␊-:␊a:aaa␊":aaa␊

// Named multiline delete goes to "1, the named register and "".
K "ad2;w X
B1 ␊0:␊1:aaa␊bbb␊-:␊a:aaa␊bbb␊":aaa␊bbb␊

## Example stated at https://github.com/kkew3/jieba.vim/issues/179#issue-6448979658
#X i

B0 |aaa␊bbb␊
K 1gg0yiw 2gg0daw X
B1 aaa␊␊0:aaa␊1:bbb␊-:bbb␊a:␊":bbb␊

// Expected behaviors:
// (CAVEAT: different from builtin behaviors, register "1 is always written)
//
// - Unnamed yank goes to "0 and "".
// - Named yank goes to the named register and "".
// - Unnamed inline delete goes to "1, "- and "".
// - Unnamed multiline delete goes to "1 and "".
// - Named inline delete goes to "1, the named register and "".
// - Named multiline delete goes to "1, the named register and "".
